    {
      "id": "f7c50e9adf6e2be3f0c0333f8c89a8fad4683985",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3055948226,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I have address 2400:3300:1:0:0:0:808:808, and I need to target 2400:3300:1:: with the ipv4 address being in the ::808:808\n\nThe current options only allow me to targe /96 with the prefix, which gets me to the ::808:808. but the only wild card options close are /64 and /32. These only allow me to targe the 2nd (/32) and 4th (/64) quartets as my ipv6 network prefix. I've added the option to configure a /48 in the wildcard options to allow for the targeting of the 3rd quartet, so an overall network ipv6 prefix of /48.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6414013,
            "username": "markspcs",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Mark Stout",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d23f12ab025d026f00225e11bfc7c32c52394e9c01f99a9f3c48a19660358bf3?s=80&d=identicon",
